      "id": "gkr9fkd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Atmospheric Pressure"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Atmospheric pressure decreases rapidly with increasing altitude as the air density reduces.",
        "The Earth features seven major pressure belts categorized into thermally formed and dynamically formed belts.",
        "Equatorial Low Pressure Belt (Doldrums) and Polar Highs are thermally induced, while Subtropical Highs and Subpolar Lows are dynamically induced.",
        "The Intertropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) is a low-pressure belt near the equator where northeast and southeast trade winds converge.",
        "Seasonal shifting of pressure belts occurs northwards and southwards following the apparent movement of the Sun."
      ],
      "id": "95ubjdn"
    },
